  "observationOnInheritedData": {
    "finding": "protected-fields.json understates the protected set by two fields.",
    "detail": "The typed binder refuses certDate and emailCB as protected_category/service_block, and the production fixtures correctly wrote neither. But field-classification.json labels certDate \"deterministic\" and emailCB \"participant\", and reports/protected-fields.json omits both from unwritableFields. A consumer reading protected-fields.json rather than production-field-map.json bindingRefusals would not learn that these two certificate-of-service fields are protected.",
    "liveRisk": "none observed in the production artifacts -- the fail-closed binder held and the service block was left entirely blank.",
    "riskIfReused": "A future lane that seeds a write set from field-classification.json class labels, rather than from bindingRefusals, could write a service date and a service-method checkbox into a certificate of service before service occurs.",
    "actionTakenHere": "Recorded only. This lane does not own the production overlay and has not modified it.",
    "carriedForward": "Both fields are marked refusedBecause service_block in the fields[] above, so this census-v1 record does not repeat the omission.",
    "statusNow": "Carried forward and independently confirmed against the binary. certDate is refused by the shared service_block name rule and emailCB by role in this family; both are blank in both rendered fixtures, proved from the artifact bytes at their measured rectangles. See reports/service-block-proof.json. The production overlay was still not modified -- this lane does not own it."
  },
  "resolution": {
    "supersededOn": "the resume build, once the corpus was recovered and source-verification.json reported verified: true",
    "supersededBy": "data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/ak/ak-tf805-set--official-pdf-fill/field-census.census-v1.json",
    "comparison": "data/rcap-all50/overlays/census-v1/ak/ak-tf805-set--official-pdf-fill/measurement-vs-inherited.json",
    "outcome": "AGREES -- all 17 fields and all 18 widgets. Every measured rectangle rounds to the inherited one, every page matches and every type matches.",
    "whyThisFileIsKept": "It is the record of what was inherited and of the custody chain behind it, and the comparison is only meaningful with it. It is NOT the geometry this family builds on: every rectangle in the census and the field map was read off the binary by this lane. An inherited number is a cross-check, never a substitute for measuring, and the direction of the comparison is inherited-checked-against-measured.",
    "whatMeasuringAddedThatInheritingCouldNot": [
      "the stroked geometry of the document -- 2 rectangles on page 1 and 9 on page 2, including the box the form draws around its certificate of service, which is what makes this family's service-block proof geometric rather than name-based",
      "the finding that pageRegions detects no region containing any widget on this document, so the region protection channel contributes nothing here",
      "the finding that the ORDER block draws four checkboxes that have no AcroForm widget at all",
      "the expansion of the `tf` service method to TrueFiling, and the five-year re-request window as attaching to Administrative Rule 40(c) only",
      "the notarial jurat on page 1, which the inherited record did not carry"
    ]
  }
